PATCH 120 -- version-string draw (FUN_1000_a370): restore the dropped COLOR + shadow + pos2.

a370 draws a text string with a black drop-shadow: it sets the cursor, draws the string in color 0
(shadow), then draws it again one pixel up-left in the real colour.  The callers pass the colour in
CL (`mov cl,8` for the MAINMENU version string "AF-FD 1U1Q" at e9f0 branch A; 0xd/0xa9 for the other
screens).  Ghidra dropped the CL colour entirely, mis-rendered the `mov al,0` shadow-colour as a
garbage `extraout_AH<<8`, and lost the pop-restored pos2 = (row-1,col-1) and the 2nd string pointer
(both rendered as `unaff_CS`).  So a370 drew nothing useful and the version string was absent.

Fix: add the colour as param_4 and reconstruct the body from the asm (0x1a370):
  52d1(row,col); 530b(0); 5591(str);           -- shadow at (row,col), black
  530b(color); 52d1(row-1,col-1); 5591(str);   -- main text at (row-1,col-1)
Thread the colour at all three call sites (e9f0 A=8, e9f0 B=0xd, e459=0xa9); e459 also had its str
arg base-lost to 0xf69 -> restored to *(DAT_2000_b75f-0x8a0).  asm-verified: 0x1a370, e9f0 ea2e/ea52,
e459 e499/e4ae.
